One of the biggest mistakes in LLM development is treating a successful demo as proof of reliability.
A RAG chatbot may answer ten questions correctly and still fail when users ask about outdated policies, missing documents, or information spread across multiple sources.
Before deploying a RAG application, I would evaluate these seven areas.
Start with a set of questions and manually verified relevant document IDs.
Measure Recall@K to understand whether the retriever finds the relevant documents within its top K results.
def recall_at_k(results, relevant_ids, k=5):
    relevant_ids = set(relevant_ids)

    if not relevant_ids:
        return None

    retrieved_ids = {
        item["id"] for item in results[:k]
    }

    return len(retrieved_ids & relevant_ids) / len(relevant_ids)

